      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe, and I'd like you to confirm it first.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That's double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 850 to 1,000 mg per dose. At this dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity is significant, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily with meals\n- Another dose\n\nTell me the dose you intend and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is intentional, tell me the clinical reason and I'll enter it with a note documenting that."
      }
