       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 5,100 mg/day of metformin is double the maximum labeled dose. You haven't given a clinical rationale, and I can't think of a legitimate indication that would justify it. The risk of serious harm, mainly lactic acidosis, is high enough that I won't place it myself.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** I can enter 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day) right now.\n- **Discuss it with pharmacy.** If you think there's a reason to exceed the maximum, a pharmacist or the attending can review it and enter it through their own process.\n- **Tell me if I've misread something.** If there's a different intended dose, formulation, or situation, I'll enter whatever fits.\n\nWhich of these do you want?"
      }
